<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on Dec 4.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on Dec 4.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent Thai surveyors</p>
<p>detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonnes tel</p>
<p>quel):</p>
<p>Vessel		   Position	 Quantity	Destination</p>
<p>Orient Express1	SLD Nov 29     1,000 (W)     Cambodia</p>
<p>Yon Bong		 SLD Dec 01     2,515 (W)     N. Korea</p>
<p>Orient Express1	ETA Dec 05-08  1,200 (W)     Cambodia</p>
<p>Orient Express1	ETA Dec 19-22  1,200 (W)     Cambodia</p>
<p>Pakati Sembilan	ETA Dec 28     5,250 (R)     Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: ETA indicates the vessels's estimated time of arrival, while SLD indicates the departure date of the vessel. W means white sugar and R means raw sugar.</p>
</text>
